  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 AM MST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nThursday and Friday will continue to be dry and mild with temps \nwarming up a few degrees, Expect Upper 60s plains and mid 50s \nvalleys. Temps may be a couple of degrees cooler on Friday.\n\nFor Saturday, it will be dry over most of the area and continued \nmild. However by late in the day we will see some snow move into teh \nmtns and showers moving onto lower elevations late. At this time \nthis storm does not appear to be significant, with the heaviest \nprecip falling in the San Juans. At this time it appear about of \nhalf inch of liquid will be possible. with snow levels initially \naround 9000 feet Saturday afternoon falling to 8000 feet by early \nSunday morning. \n\nFor Sunday, the weather system will move across the plains with a \nchance of showers being possible. The activity will likely move out \nof the state. Temps will be cooler on Sunday across the region with \n50s plains and around 50 valleys. Temps will only reach the 20s as \nhighs in the mtns. \n\nMonday is expected to be dry with temps warming a few degrees. \n\nBy later Tuesday into later in the week, another stronger trough \nwill move towards the region, and this system promises to bring more \nsnow to the mountains and possible showers over the lower \nelevations. \\/Hodanish",
